  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday morning through next Monday)\nIssued at 208 PM EST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nThe extended periods begin Thu morning with the frontal boundary \nnearly stalled across the area. The front should be somewhere near \nan ATL to CSG line and it does not make much SERLY progress through \nThu night. This will keep at least chance PoPs across the CWA through \nFri morning/early afternoon. A second dry frontal boundary pushes \ninto NW GA Fri afternoon and pushes the 1st boundary out of the \nregion Fri night. The bulk of the precip is expected to fall Wed/Wed \nnight but we should still see an additional 0.1\" to 0.5\" across the \narea Thu to Fri morning.  The better instability values and dynamics \nwith this system stay well north of the state along the front as it \nmoves east through the Mid-Atlantic states. Widespread severe \nweather is not expected. \n\nThis system finally pushes south of the state just before daybreak \nSat as another high pressure ridge begins to build into the \nsoutheastern U.S. from the Northern/Central Plains. This will cool \nthings of a bit as we get into the beginning of next week. \n\nTemperatures will be mainly in the 70s to lower 80s through Friday \nwith highs cooling into the 60s and 70s Sat/Sun. Low temps expected \nin the 50s and 60s through Fri with lows in the 40s and 50s Sat/Sun. \nMay even see some upper 30s across the NE GA mountains Sun night.",
